104	 * REAL INCIDENT (2026-07-26 customer-journey rehearsal, H2). The card-paid deploy
105	 * path quoted a total, charged the CARD its share of that total at Stripe, and
106	 * then — on the confirm redirect, minutes or hours later — re-ran `orderQuote`
107	 * and debited whatever came back. That re-run includes `currentPromo(new Date())`,
108	 * and lib/promotions.ts always has an active sale that rotates by calendar date,
109	 * so a rotation between "customer clicked Deploy" and "customer came back from
110	 * Stripe" re-priced the order AFTER the card had cleared and took the difference
111	 * out of the wallet with no new consent. With no balance to take it from, the
112	 * payment was captured and no server was created.
113	 *
114	 * `lib/resize.ts` and `lib/disk-expand.ts` already carried the amount through
115	 * Stripe metadata for exactly this reason; the order path was the one that
116	 * re-derived it. Same rule as lib/renewal-quote.ts and lib/proration.ts: a figure
117	 * the customer was shown is not recomputed later, it is carried.
118	 *
119	 * `promoPercent` and `promoName` travel WITH the total because they are not
120	 * decoration. `Server.termPromoPercent` records the rate a term was actually sold
121	 * at (every later proration prices against it), and the promo name is the ledger
122	 * and invoice text the customer reads. Honouring a 30%-off price while stamping
123	 * today's 15% would hand every later proration the wrong basis and print a
124	 * discount on the invoice that does not match the money taken.
