128	 * Safe to call repeatedly and concurrently from the redirect and the webhook.
129	 *
130	 * THROWS when Stripe cannot be read. That is deliberate and it is the fix for the
131	 * defect found on 2026-07-27: this function used to ask three helpers for the
132	 * session, each of which swallowed every error into `null`, so a transient Stripe
133	 * failure was indistinguishable from "no purchase metadata" and fell through to
134	 * the top-up branch below reporting `fulfilled: true`. A real order then had its
135	 * card charged with no server, no FulfilledSession row and no notification — and
136	 * because the webhook returns 200 either way, Stripe never retried it. A throw
137	 * lands the browser on `?pending=1` (see app/api/stripe/confirm) and puts the
138	 * failure in the webhook's log, which is loud; declaring it a top-up was silent.
139	 */
140	export async function fulfilCheckoutSession(sessionId: string, base = ""): Promise<FulfilResult> {
